			<div class="content" id="post-content-4817878">
									

<p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Seeking Greenlights:</span></strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Page Type:</span></strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Genre:</span></strong> Emotional, Comedy</p>
<p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Elevator Pitch:</span></strong> A cast iron kitchen set, comprising of a Stove, Refrigerator, and Kitchen Sink, is haunted by a loving spirit. It will cook for people and produces food that heals. However, one rule, never look inside the cabinets nor pots of the kitchen. The specter will chase and beat, with a wooden spoon, any one who breaks their rules.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+Open&nbsp;removed&nbsp;item</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-Close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Object Description Summary:</span></strong> A cast iron kitchen set, consisting of a Stove, Refrigerator, and Kitchen Sink from the turn of the 19th century. When a person is within the room, or 30 meters, of these objects, a spectral humanoid appears at the stove. It is accompanied by spectral pots and pans and the smell of cooking food. The specter appears to be a elderly women of the same race as the observer. The specter will cook and produce any food the person asks for. This food has healing properties for both the mind and body. However, there is one rule of her kitchen, never look or reach into the pots on the stove nor in the cabinets. The specter will become angry and will proceed to chase and beat the transgressor with a wooden spoon until the specter feels that they have learned a lesson.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
<strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Central Narrative:</span></strong> The main plot point; this kitchen set houses, if not traps, a benevolent spirit that only wants to help those around it. The specter views other humans as their children and wants to protect them.
<p>This object is inhabited by a specter. It has attached and or merged with the anomalous effects of the kitchen set. Through notes, interviews, and addendums the specter's past will be revealed. Through incident reports, the beneficial and negative affects of the object will be revealed. The benefits will range from healing to protection. But the negative will range from light injury to near-keter events. The Spirit and the objects are separate.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+Narrative&nbsp;Outline</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-Close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<ol>
<li>First interview (Generic Questions about origins of SCP and Specter)
<ol>
<li>Details where the SCP was found and the most recent things the Specter Remembers</li>
</ol>
</li>
<li>Second Interview (Questions about the Specter's past and her rules)
<ol>
<li>Show the cooking ability of the Specter and the fact that the interviewer enjoyed the time.</li>
</ol>
</li>
<li>Incident one (When SCP-2 and SCP-3 manifest and attack a armed guard.)
<ol>
<li>Include audio and video transcript of the incident and the addendum for containment</li>
</ol>
</li>
<li>Incident two (The first time that the specter protected a foundation member from another SCP)
<ol>
<li>Include audio and video transcript of the incident</li>
</ol>
</li>
<li>Third Interview (Establish more history and where the Specter is from and how she meet the SCP)
<ol>
<li>Reveal Specter's tragic history and the possible origin of the SCP</li>
<li>Reveal the origins of SCP-2 and SCP-3</li>
</ol>
</li>
<li>Experiment 1 / Incident three expand on what is inside of SCP and why the specter does not want anyone to look inside. Humanize the specter further and give a good reason why the researchers take it's feelings into consideration
<ol>
<li>Include transcripts</li>
</ol>
</li>
</ol>
<p>More will come as I write the article and become inspired.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Hook/Attention-Grabber:</span></strong> Specter of indeterminate race will cook for you as long as you do not snoop in their kitchen.</p>
<p>This SCP provides a great service to it's Site. However, the positive effects comes with strict rules and consequences. But not deadly consequences.</p>
<p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Additional Notes:</span></strong> This is my very first SCP Concept post.</p>

