				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/quadraginta" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6391595); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6391595&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605926500" alt="Quadraginta" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6391595)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/quadraginta" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6391595); return false;" >Quadraginta</a></span> <span class="odate time_1605728866 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">18 Nov 2020 19:47</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4821837">
									

<p>I absolutely adore the <strong>Elevator Pitch</strong> and think that a loving grandma ghost is just the sweetest thing in a long time.</p>
<p>However, I'd like the <strong>Central Narrative</strong> to actually tell me a specific series of events instead of just telling me that addendums, incidents, etc. will show us things happening.</p>
<p>Just as a regular book has chapters and pages, scp articles have addendums, incidents, logs, etc.</p>
<p>Also, I'd remove the <strong>Object Description Summary</strong> as the elevator pitch already stated everything we need to know, anomaly-wise.</p>
<p>Plot-wise, I just wanna know who or what this benevolent entity is and/or why she doesn't want people to look in the pot stove or cabinets&#8230; what're you hidin', granny?</p>

							</div>

								
					
